# Web boundaries
- Implement customer/pro UI, auth/session, uploads, intent entry, job status and result rendering only. Keep model calls, document extraction, study merge, and domain rules out of the web runtime.
- Enforce server-side ownership/access on every API and storage operation; never trust client-provided user/Hive identifiers without authorization checks. Never expose service-role keys in browser bundles.
- Display uncertainty, failure/retry states and evidence links honestly; generated reports must identify source study revision. Follow `reference/HiveForYou brand guide.pdf` when available, including accessible semantic colors and source chips.
- Web requests/events carry scoped IDs, not raw private documents or model prompts. Show actionable errors without leaking implementation details.
